kely to be beaten (since higher pairs are costly), and gives me a high chance of retaining control without wasting a bomb or high single.\n\nReason: Leading with the pair ♠3 ♣3 maximizes the chance to retain initiative while conserving high-value singles like ♥2 and ♠K for future tricks. It is low enough that opponents are unlikely to waste valuable pairs to beat it, especially since the next player (Right) has only 6 cards and likely wants to preserve playable combinations. This move maintains tempo and reduces my hand efficiently.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠3", "♣3"]}'}
